WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.580
The echo is gone.

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.340
Then a new route opens to the east,

3
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.220
through old cable and a smoothing circuit.

4
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:06.880
Nothing drops, nothing buzzes.

5
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:07.900
Yet the tickets say:

6
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.360
it's like talking through a wall.

7
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.200
Every word is there,

8
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.320
but its edges are gone.

9
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.320
The route is linear and time-invariant,

10
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.920
so do what lesson two taught you:

11
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.420
send one click and listen.

12
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.400
It comes back smeared
across three samples:

13
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.840
point one five, point seven,

14
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:21.640
point one five.

15
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.820
But nowhere in those numbers
is the word muffled.

16
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.260
We need a different question.

17
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.020
So feed it one steady tone:

18
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.200
two thousand hertz.

19
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.640
At eight thousand samples a second,

20
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.160
that's one, zero, minus one, zero.

21
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:32.920
What comes out?

22
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.940
The same pattern,
shrunk to seventy percent,

23
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:35.800
one sample late.

24
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.820
A tone went in,
and the same tone came out.

25
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:38.900
Why?

26
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.480
Picture a dot on the rim of a wheel.

27
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.620
The sample is how far left or
right it sits.

28
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.480
Those samples are the dot turning
ninety degrees every sample.

29
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.900
One thousand hertz turns
forty-five degrees.

30
00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.240
Four thousand turns half a turn,

31
00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.360
so its samples flip.

32
00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.640
That's the tone as a wheel.

33
00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.770
The route's output is the same dot,

34
00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.090
only smaller and behind.

35
00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.170
How much a system scales
one tone is its gain.

36
00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.210
Here, point seven.

37
00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:02.070
How many degrees the output's dot trails
the input's is its phase. Here, ninety.

38
00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.850
Why does every tone come out as itself?

39
00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.830
The route adds three copies of the input:

40
00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:07.930
fresh, one sample old,

41
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:08.950
two samples old.

42
00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.630
Draw each as an arrow
scaled by its weight,

43
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:11.910
and add them tip to tail.

44
00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:12.790
As the wheel turns,

45
00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:13.970
all three arrows turn together,

46
00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.930
so their sum turns at the same speed.

47
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.190
No new tone can appear.

48
00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:21.150
Now sweep the tone from zero
to four thousand hertz.

49
00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.610
Zero keeps one hundred percent.

50
00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:24.190
Two thousand keeps seventy.

51
00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.830
Four thousand, only forty.

52
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.370
Gain and phase, for every tone:

53
00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.970
that's the frequency response.

54
00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:30.390
And there's the wall.

55
00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:31.970
Vowels live low and walk through.

56
00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.870
The edges of consonants
live near three thousand,

57
00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:35.750
where the route keeps less than half.

58
00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.070
Turn up the volume?

59
00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:40.270
Doubling everything keeps the proportions:

60
00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:43.170
three thousand hertz still comes out
half as strong as five hundred.

61
00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:46.390
And the loudest callers get pushed
past the line's range and clip.

62
00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:49.210
One knob can't fix tones
scaled by different amounts.

63
00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:50.520
Here's the fix.

64
00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.900
The route keeps seventy percent
of two thousand hertz,

65
00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.200
so boost that tone
by one over point seven:

66
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.120
one point four three.

67
00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:57.700
Do it band by band,

68
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.280
each band a stretch
of neighboring tones with one knob,

69
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.900
and every tone gets out at full strength.

70
00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.000
The caller steps out from behind the wall.

71
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.300
Then a hearing clinic files a ticket.

72
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.060
They play a whistle
at five thousand hertz,

73
00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.240
and patients hear a clean three thousand.

74
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.180
Our wheel stopped at four thousand.

75
00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.640
What happens to a dot that turns
more than half a turn per sample?
